            <ArticleTitle>An obese young man with uncontrolled diabetes and insatiable hunger: Prader-Willi syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S680-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/2230-8210.123566</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Prader-Willi syndrome (PWS) is a rare cause of obesity. With the rising incidence of obesity, clinicians need to be aware of genetic causes of obesity and when to suspect them. A case of PWS, which was diagnosed in adulthood, has been discussed. This case is special because of lack of history of floppiness in infancy and predominance behavioral problems.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
